nyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414640#post1414640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that if you provide an answer rather than let PCs work it out for themselves that you've done a poor job as an ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you allow Paths of Enlightenment and their Virtues to remove the Tenets system completely? (Because I have playtested them as Tenets, and they do not work.) And you don't let PCs know the basic assumptions of the Chronicle? Because I have never enjoyed an Anarchs game in over 20 years, the closest was Autarkis at points during the Giovanni Chronicles.<br /> <br /> To me the 'other side' is the Anarchs and Cam. They may even be the enemy, but that might be the other Packs, depending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 09-19-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T14:00:24-07:00","id":1414643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414634#post1414634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, they're humans called vampires.<br /> <br /> And before you say all the superpowers make them not human, almost all of them can be done by humans called mages.<br /> <br /> And every human being can become that.</div> </div> </div> </div>even mages have a name for humans...sleepers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T14:01:39-07:00","id":1414644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414641#post1414641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you allow Paths of Enlightenment and their Virtues to remove the Tenets system completely? (Because I have playtested them as Tenets, and they do not work.) And you don't let PCs know the basic assumptions of the Chronicle? Because I have never enjoyed an Anarchs game in over 20 years, the closest was Autarkis at points during the Giovanni Chronicles.<br /> <br /> To me the 'other side' is the Anarchs and Cam. They may even be the enemy, but that might be the other Packs, depending.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't use either system. I find the system the least important part of the game and rarely bother with doing anything more than keep a vague track of Humanity and Path scores when running games. I generally run a bit like Jason Carl in that the system is there but I only call for rolls at dramatically important time.<br /> <br /> How do I run morality in V5? I ask the players to describe their Morality System and then make a score of it. Then if they violate that morality then they lose a point. Sometimes if dramatically appropriate, I let them gain a point.<br /> <br /> It's more or less identical to the way I ran Paths, Roads, and Humanity.<br /> <br /> Roads and Paths are not something to mechanize anymore than you should care about Alignment in D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T14:05:35-07:00","id":1414645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414644#post1414644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't use either system. I find the system the least important part of the game and rarely bother with doing anything more than keep a vague track of Humanity and Path scores when running games. I generally run a bit like Jason Carl in that the system is there but I only call for rolls at dramatically important time.<br /> <br /> How do I run morality in V5? I ask the players to describe their Morality System and then make a score of it. Then if they violate that morality then they lose a point. Sometimes if dramatically appropriate, I let them gain a point.<br /> <br /> It's more or less identical to the way I ran Paths, Roads, and Humanity.<br /> <br /> Roads and Paths are not something to mechanize anymore than you should care about Alignment in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I am way more simulationist than that, I find it really helps to seperate character ability from player ability, especially when the shy player wants to play a charismatic or charming character, or the natural salesman the charmless thug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T14:46:08-07:00","id":1414655,"title":"","content":"pretty evil, but never irrationally evil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:29:40-07:00","id":1414660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tWYCS6k1IOA\" data-code=\"tWYCS6k1IOA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tWYCS6k1IOA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T19:15:46-07:00","id":1414677,"title":"","content":"The problem is that evil is more or less a meaningless concept. One groups Hero/Rebel is another groups Terrorist/Criminal and thus evil comes down to if the individual or group is working towards a goal you agree with.<br /> <br /> In TV shows like Burn Notice, Leverage, and Person of Interest, the &quot;good guys&quot; routinely manipulate the &quot;bad guys&quot; into defeating themselves, often with lethal results. Conversely in the Hannibal tv series we often see that Hannibal manipulates things from the shadows for no greater good than his own amusement and curiosity. Then you have the hybrid 2013 tv series of <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt2296682/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_8\" target=\"_blank\">Dracula</a> which tried to have Dracula be a sympathetic figure who is trying to take on a corrupt secret society by being essentially as bad as they are, all the while claiming the moral high ground.<br /> <br /> In the gaming groups I used to run with the characters were more or less the types that killed when required to survive or advance their plans. But needless killing was boring and tended to be viewed as sloppy. Not unlike the Kindred of the East take on how to behave actually, but we generally played V:tM.<br /> <br /> Considering the body counts that some game groups can produce it might be a good idea to try to classify players as serial killer types, rather than inherently good vs. evil in nature. Most of the players in my groups tended to fall into the &quot;mission based killer&quot; archetype. They have a job or mission to carry out and if you get in the way they may kill you or they may ignore you based on the mission requirements. I suspect this is a more common response in Players if only because the way the game mechanics are designed, they support a win/fail state of play, thus the group will try to win the game. Thankfully the number of players who had personal issues where they wanted to experiment with behaviors that would fall under other killer types were rare. <br /> <br /> In a strange twist I have to admit that one of the lowest body count games I played in was an all Assamite coterie game. Each character was a specialist in a different form of killing, be it at range, melee, poisons, accidents, etc. But since they were only paid to kill the main target, there was no incentive to Rambo their way through dozens or hundreds of body guards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T19:31:19-07:00","id":1414678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414677#post1414677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that evil is more or less a meaningless concept. One groups Hero/Rebel is another groups Terrorist/Criminal and thus evil comes down to if the individual or group is working towards a goal you agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a meaningless concept unless you believe that someone ascribing meaning to it counts. In which case it becomes ALL meaning.<br /> <br /> Just because it's only your conception of good and evil doesn't make it any less valuable because you're the only head that matters. Its the one under your control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T20:13:29-07:00","id":1414683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414678#post1414678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a meaningless concept unless you believe that someone ascribing meaning to it counts. In which case it becomes ALL meaning.<br /> <br /> Just because it's only your conception of good and evil doesn't make it any less valuable because you're the only head that matters. Its the one under your control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anyone can believe anything, but it doesn't matter unless they have the power to influence others to make those beliefs count.<br /> <br /> For example if a moderator bans some one for bringing up a given topic, it doesn't matter if the Moderator was righteously upholding the rules or suppressing free speech in an evil way. It only matters in the end that the moderator had the power and chose to use it. The morality of a given action tends to be retroactively filled in hindsight with justifications or excuses. Kind of like how historical figures go through waves of revisionism based upon which political or moral view is currently in public favor.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to get into a discussion about validating other peoples views, that opens up a completely different can of worms due to the motivation of why you validate them. For some people they can not conceive of not validating everyone. For other people you validate other peoples views only so far as to understand their mental limitations and how to manipulate them. But then that gets compounded by what they choose to do if anything with that insight. Then you have people that don't have enough coffee in their systems to care one way or another.<br /> <br /> Sadly a lot of people tend to knee jerk react to buzz words like &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; without ever really questioning what makes them fall into those categories. It wouldn't be far off to suggest that many aspects of &quot;morality&quot; are like loot boxes in modern video games, you are told repeatedly that you want the stuff in the loot boxes to the point that you sink untold hours and or huge amounts of currency into pursuing the contents, but along the way few people want to ask if they should really be playing the game at all, let alone if the loot boxes are worth it.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I agree with the OP that there is no right answer to this concept. But I do point to the fact that since there is no right answer, the concepts of &quot;good/evil&quot; can't be taken as absolute values, especially since the collective views on such things change over time and is so dependent on context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T20:17:43-07:00","id":1414684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414683#post1414683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anyone can believe anything, but it doesn't matter unless they have the power to influence others to make those beliefs count.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least everyone has the ability to make their beliefs count for themselves.<br /> <br /> A Malkavian may believe a Stop Sign talks to him and his TV but if that guy slaughters the Prince of Los Angeles, he's made his ridiculous beliefs count.<br /> <br /> Certainly despite its immaterialness, good vs. evil has an enormous impact on Kindred society as it defines, &quot;What do I believe? What will I do? What won't I do? How far do I hold the Beast at bay.&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's just my two cents.<br /> <br /> Also, it certainly DOES influence how groups like the Anarchs fight the Camarilla as they are NOT the good guys but they certainly believe they are.<br /> <br /> My .02.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T21:01:21-07:00","id":1414686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414684#post1414684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the very least everyone has the ability to make their beliefs count for themselves.<br /> <br /> A Malkavian may believe a Stop Sign talks to him and his TV but if that guy slaughters the Prince of Los Angeles, he's made his ridiculous beliefs count.<br /> <br /> Certainly despite its immaterialness, good vs. evil has an enormous impact on Kindred society as it defines, &quot;What do I believe? What will I do? What won't I do? How far do I hold the Beast at bay.&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's just my two cents.<br /> <br /> Also, it certainly DOES influence how groups like the Anarchs fight the Camarilla as they are NOT the good guys but they certainly believe they are.<br /> <br /> My .02.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Though the Malkavian concept does bring up an interesting parallel. Most societies agree that love is a good thing, But if the individual is suffering from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erotomania\" target=\"_blank\">Erotomania</a> that &quot;good&quot; thing called love drives the individual to extreme behaviors that can create a lot of &quot;evil&quot;. We as a society find the results of this behavior abhorrent, thus classify it as a mental disorder, allowing us to maintain a clean distinction between good and evil, regardless of the hair we end up splitting to make it work.<br /> <br /> In regards to the anarchs, they have always struck me as individuals who think in binary terms. In the early days of television and movies there were a lot of westerns made. Due to poor image quality and the black and white film stock, people making the shows started using visual short hand to assist the audience follow what was happening on screen. The hero would wear a white cowboy hat, while the villains wore black cowboy hats. This is where our hacking and character terms of &quot;white hat or black hat&quot; come from.<br /> <br /> The anarchs are the type of people who look in the mirror and say &quot;since I am not wearing a black hat, I can't be a bad guy, thus since I am not a bad guy, I must be a good guy&quot;. Completely ignoring the flaw in the thinking that an absence of obvious evil means a default state of grace. This lack of awareness is shown by the character of Charlette Richards in the Lucifer series when she says &quot;why would I go to hell, I pay my taxes and I work hard&quot; while simultaneously ensuring murderers escape justice.<br /> <br /> But in theory if we agree that an absence of obvious evil does not make one good, then an absence of an obvious good does not make one evil either.<br /> <br /> Once we start down this particular rabbit hole of thought, then we have to start taking into account things like virtue signalling and societal good vs. the individual good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T01:10:33-07:00","id":1414700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414625#post1414625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, I think you can divide characters into five &quot;morality ratings.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Good guy vampires.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Average guy vampires.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Jerks.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Assholes.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Monsters.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. I like this enough that I'm going to steal it and save me the work of describing things.<br /> <br /> I went through my NPC portfolio for my game, and here's where the breakdown was, by clan:<br /> <br /> BRUJAH:<br /> Good Guys: 2<br /> Average Guys: 9<br /> Jerks: 3<br /> Assholes: 6<br /> Monsters: 1<br /> <br /> GANGREL:<br /> Good Guys: 0<br /> Average Guys: 3<br /> Jerks: 3<br /> Assholes: 4<br /> Monsters: 0<br /> <br /> MALKAVIANS:<br /> Good Guys: 1<br /> Average Guys: 2<br /> Jerks: 3<br /> Assholes: 3<br /> Monsters: 2<br /> <br /> NOSFERATU:<br /> Good Guys: 3<br /> Average Guys: 2<br /> Jerks: 4<br /> Assholes: 4<br /> Monsters: 0<br /> <br /> TOREADOR:<br /> Good Guys: 1<br /> Average Guys: 5<br /> Jerks: 7<br /> Assholes: 4<br /> Monsters: 0<br /> <br /> TREMERE:<br /> Good Guys: 1<br /> Average Guys: 5<br /> Jerks: 5<br /> Assholes: 5<br /> Monsters: 0<br /> <br /> VENTRUE:<br /> Good Guys: 2<br /> Average Guys: 7<br /> Jerks: 5<br /> Assholes: 7<br /> Monsters: 1<br /> <br /> TOTALS:<br /> Good Guys: 10<br /> Average Guys: 33<br /> Jerks: 30<br /> Assholes: 33<br /> Monsters: 4<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414625#post1414625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Chronicle Ratings</b></u><br /> Broadly speaking, I think there is a spectrum that chronicles fall into. Also with one to five dots because hey, it's the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have thought I was running a V/20-2e Chronicle based on your description. Maybe I still do, but the fact that my Good Guys outnumber my monsters by more than a factor of two gives me pause. A lot of the moral thematics you describe, though, fit my game to a Tee -- particularly with everything being potentially sinister underneath.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T02:04:12-07:00","id":1414703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414700#post1414700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went through my NPC portfolio for my game, and here's where the breakdown was, by clan:</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, fun. <br /> <br /> Let's crunch the numbers some more. Good Guys are worth 1 point, Monsters 5, rest in between. Divide the total rating by the number of vamps to get an average.<br /> <br /> Bruah: 2.7. Average Guys.<br /> Gangrel: 3.1. Jerks. <br /> Malks: 3.3. Jerks.<br /> Nos: 3.2. Jerks.<br /> Toreador: 2.8. Average Guys.<br /> Tremere: 2.9. Average Guys.<br /> Ventrue: 2.9. Average Guys.<br /> <br /> Total Average: 2.97867. Your vampires are Average Guys just a hair short of being Jerks, if we don't round up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would have thought I was running a V/20-2e Chronicle based on your description. Maybe I still do, but the fact that my Good Guys outnumber my monsters by more than a factor of two gives me pause. A lot of the moral thematics you describe, though, fit my game to a Tee -- particularly with everything being potentially sinister underneath. </div> </div> </div>By the numbers, your chronicle is there, if Vampions is 1, 1e/2e is 2, and V20/2e is 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T08:49:33-07:00","id":1414744,"title":"","content":"I like the mix. Player characters tend towards the Good Guy and Average Guy side, and I do this myself unless I'm making a point to play a Jerk or worse. I usually have worse-than-average vampires in positions of power, because vampire society is a lot like organised crime.<br /> <br /> It also varies with chronicles. Sometimes I lean heavily into the organised crime side where noblest motivation available is revenge, and sometimes the gloomy philosophy and soul-searching about whether this existence can be justified.<br /> <br /> I will generally make Good Guy an active choice, and generally not an easy one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:49:51-07:00","id":1414759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414634#post1414634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, they're humans called vampires.<br /> <br /> And before you say all the superpowers make them not human, almost all of them can be done by humans called mages.<br /> <br /> And every human being can become that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awakened aren't humans either and not every human can awaken to do True Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:19:28-07:00","id":1414765,"title":"","content":"i think it depends on the group you play with and what people enjoy mostly.<br /> <br /> that being said i think most vampires fall into the Evil category from a D&amp;D point of view. At the end of day all vampires commit crimes a lot (so not lawful either though yu may say adhearing to the camarilla laws is a new kind of lawful evil)<br /> <br /> Most of kindred society is chaotic evil - the strongest rule and everything else is just a tool you use. thats most vampires in my book. Then ofc there is the beast and the slow decay of ones humanity. If vampires werent evil they wouldnt have that struggle in the first place. But you will kill people. Regularely. For egoistic reasonsor accidents.<br /> <br /> You could say, that some clans are wayyyyy more evil than others so the D&amp;D chart doesnt quite apply cause clearly a Tzimisce is many levels of evil more evil than a Salubri. A Nagaraja or Setite is clearly deeper down the evil path than a Ventrue or Toreador. And ofc a Tremere is way more lawfull than a Brujah<br /> <br /> But as Bertram in Bloodlines 1 says - none of us are the good guys here.<br /> <br /> So yes all kindred are evil. Some are more monstrous than others though and i think its fitting to represent that. A Toreador might at least try to keep up his humanity, while Tzimisce try their best to get rid of theirs. Sure a Lasombra might slip into debauchery but at least they arent trying to spread corruption like the Setites.<br /> Sure a Giovanni is kinda f*ed up in the head but its not a Baali...<br /> <br /> A thing that bothers me mostly is the common portrayal of 2 clans: Malkavian and Baali.<br /> The former are amongst the most frightening creepy clan of all. Because Mental Illness combined with the beast is NOT funny, its not hilarious, its not Whacky. Imagine a legit psychopath barely holding it together and then you wear a blue jacket to a meeting which is his trigger and he just rips your head off cause you wore the wrong color shirt. You may whisper a word that makes him snap. or worse...the VOICES may make the Malkavian snap and run Amok.<br /> Malkavians are unpredictable lethal predators you can not trust. They are mentally unwell in the same way Hannibal lecter and other serial killers were.<br /> <br /> The Latter is in my oppinion way too often abused as just a run of the mill villain who is all about being evil for the sake of being evil, with little to no strategy just powerhouses for an interesting combat encounter who behave like stupid grunts. A shovelhead with an upgrade.<br /> While Nergali ARE arrogant and powerhungry and evil for the sake of ascending to demonhood, there is more Baali variants than those idiots - whose arrogance almost wiped them from the face of the earth 3 times now.<br /> <br /> The swarm / unnamed can be a very great introduction into deeper Lore, the paranormal and just absolutely horryfing creepyness. Disease, insects, spiders, hdden deep underground with rotting corpses that breed dangerous rodents? yeah they can make for a setting that make Tzimisce havens look nice and cozy. They also go well with crossovers as Annanasi (fera / werespiders) cooperate with them and they serve the wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Azaneali are best imagined as evil mysticists willing to side and sell everything to gain knowledge and power. They are the only baali that acutally have pitch black eyes and crooked teeth due to their transformation in chorazon. They align with demons AND the abyss they have Daimonion AND obtenebration. FEAR them. They are the closest to Nephandi the vampire franchise has to offer. They are a great source of making Tremere ashamed of their lack of achievements. And while nephandi rrely interact with vampires, if they do, the Azaneali are perfect to bringing up the most evil villains of any fantasy game ever.<br /> <br /> The Molochim are my personal favorite because they take the title &quot;Baali&quot; (Lords) the most serious. they want to rule vampire society like vampires rule mortal society. They want ultimately to rule the world. But that means they are the least likely to enter pacts, they will prefer to enslave demons cause a ruler shouldnt be in debt to someone else. They also dont want the world destroyed, they keep the earthbound asleep cause ruling over ashes isnt quite intruiging. They play the double masquerade infiltrating the other clans like those infiltrate mortal society, corrupting kindred like setites, leading them down a dark path until there is nor eturn and making them full Baali by apostasy, gaining more influence.<br /> The Molochim did side with the Tal mahe Ra (true black hand) and even are at war with the Nergali and responsiblefor 2 of the 3 total wars against the Nergali that united all clans.<br /> Molochim are great for conspiracies and some weir dcreepy things that arent exactly wrong but you cant ut your finger on it. in special for tremere players the order of the wyrm baali / Molochim can be very intruiging encounters. But for any vampire, seeing that your only actual friend in this world or that Elder you like so much is actually a Baali can be very interesting for RP.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile there is also different ASPECTS of evil - Tzimisce arent so corrupting and lieing as Setites, not paying intrigues like Toreador, but their cruelty with Viscissitude surpasses even the Baali. The ventrue are powerhungry bastards but not willing to go as far as the Tremere, and the Giovanni and Nagaraja are just on a different level alltogether. The baali jsut have alla spects of evil in them but i wouldnt say they are the worst at any of them despite infernalism ^^<br /> <br /> That said Evil is a moral judgement made by a society. many things we deem evil in the west, are of and fine in the east. And many things that are unspeakable in the east are totally ok here.<br /> We today think of many things as utterly evil that were absolutely normal or even praised as virtue in the past and likely, mankind in the future will say we today were utterly evil and corrupt.<br /> <br /> And its a thing of context. Killing a human is evil. is it under all circumstances? What if it is a mass murderer trying to kell 100 people you could save by shooting them? Ah context changes everything.<br /> <br /> So ofc. HUMANS would deem most things vampires do as evil. But vampires? i guess they have a way more lenient interpretation of what is actually evil. Drinking dry a human? ah well happens. Drinking dry a vampire? Now you are evil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 09-20-2020, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:23:02-07:00","id":1414766,"title":"","content":"I've twelve players generally in two groups of six, with two irregular players. In my Chicago Chronicles, We have humanist chronicle tenets.. A PC can have whatever convictions they like, even those that duplicate &quot;paths of enlightenment&quot;, and what we've found is that the PCs sort of &quot;settle&quot; at specific humanity levels, I've one PC who's managed to maintain a humanity of 8. I've another who suffered a humanity loss early in the chronicle, but hasn't since, and has a humanity of 7. The majority of PCs have a humanity of 4-5. I've two PCs with a humanity of 3, and one with a humanity of 2. Interstngly, its my older, veteran players who play the most monstrous of PCs (jaded, cynical players of the Jyhad that they are). My younger players, are more the opposite. Relative to the SPCs in the game, I can genuinely say, they're still less monstrous than some of the SPCs. The PC with the 2 humanity? He's probably come the closest to being as bad as some of the worse SPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:59:34-07:00","id":1414772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414759#post1414759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Awakened aren't humans either and not every human can awaken to do True Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every human has an Avatar.<br /> <br /> What's your take on humans with Numina?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:06:44-07:00","id":1414773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414772#post1414772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every human has an Avatar.<br /> <br /> What's your take on humans with Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>do you think you'd be the same man if you had magic? if you could bend reality?<br /> do you think you'd be the same man if you didn't age, if you couldn't enjoy hamburgers, if you couldn't get any more new ideas for your novels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:11:12-07:00","id":1414777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414773#post1414773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> do you think you'd be the same man if you had magic? if you could bend reality?<br /> do you think you'd be the same man if you didn't age, if you couldn't enjoy hamburgers, if you couldn't get any more new ideas for your novels?</div> </div> </div> </div>All abilities change a person.<br /> <br /> I don't see magic as fundamentally different from any other skill.<br /> <br /> I don't think Humans with Numina are monsters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:25:08-07:00","id":1414780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414777#post1414777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All abilities change a person.<br /> <br /> I don't see magic as fundamentally different from any other skill.<br /> <br /> I don't think Humans with Numina are monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>as far as WoD goes, science and technology are simply consensual magic<br /> <br /> but here's the thing, scientists and other traditional mages and numina users all have differenet moralities,<br /> they each have their own versions of what's right and wrong and, while they do overlap in certain areas, we don't expect them to agree on what's morally acceptable<br /> <br /> the same way, humans of today and humans of ages past have different moralities,<br /> a couple of decades back, no one would expect recieving a phone call from me,<br /> but now that cell phones are verywhere, not calling them paints me as an antisocial lunatic to them (real story)<br /> <br /> the same way, vampires who are forced to drink blood, don't age and don't mature, lose creativity and can never see the light of day have different morals...or at least they should<br /> <br /> the fact that vampires are subject to the same mores as humans is nonesensical,<br /> it makes sense for them to adopt humanity to fight back their feral nature,<br /> but to say that they are the same as human and what is considered good and bad matches the perceptions of humans is nonesensical<br /> <br /> vampires aren't humans, vampires are a creature using human moralities or transhuman ones to fight off the beast,<br /> they are not humans, they are masquerading as humans,<br /> it's in the name ffs: Vampire : The Masquerade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:37:05-07:00","id":1414782,"title":"","content":"For my own PCs and PCs at my game table (whether I play or ST), most PCs tend to want to achieve some sort of goal or power, which means they'll eventually use force or violence to accomplish it (even if only as defense against someone who will actively strive to prevent them from achieving that). So Humanity tends to be driven down to 4 by the end of the chronicle, in some cases to 3. It almost always tend to settle between 4-5. I've only seen it go lower than that when something unexpected happens in game, and the player reluctantly decides to send his character down a dark path that will lead to his destruction (usually because of revenge). But there's never been a starting character concept like that.<br /> <br /> I've had players express to be interested in playing a vampire who retains a high Humanity, the problem is that the game's plots tend to derail that. No matter how sympathetic the ST is to that concept; typically the only thing to do involves violence. There is not much for a high Humanity PC to do except take themselves out of the game (the rest of the coterie can do that, but I'll sit here and not do anything for several hours until they're done) and be bored for a lot of the game. Since that defeats the purpose of playing the game, players ether abandon a good guy concept or never play one. They want to have fun and do stuff. This is a statement more about the limits of the STs rather than the PCs, but it is an ongoing problem.<br /> <br /> The one thing I do notice is that should an NPC do anything to humiliate one of the PCs, the PC will almost always allow their Humanity to fall in order to get revenge on that NPC - particularly by killing the NPC. Players really, really hate being humiliated in game. They will hate the NPC that did it with a passion that exceeds their distate for NPCs that are by far morally worse.<br /> <br /> As for NPCs, every group of NPCs will be at a spectrum. There's essentially no moral difference between the Camarilla and Anarchs. Except that in the Camarilla, low Humanity vampires tend to be older, and among the Anarchs low Humanity vampires tend to be younger. It all depends on who wants power bad enough. The Sabbat though has a much more worse moral spectrum than the others. The Independent Clans tend to be worse than the Camarilla/Anarchs too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:41:44-07:00","id":1414831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414782#post1414782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had players express to be interested in playing a vampire who retains a high Humanity, the problem is that the game's plots tend to derail that. No matter how sympathetic the ST is to that concept; typically the only thing to do involves violence. There is not much for a high Humanity PC to do except take themselves out of the game (the rest of the coterie can do that, but I'll sit here and not do anything for several hours until they're done) and be bored for a lot of the game. Since that defeats the purpose of playing the game, players ether abandon a good guy concept or never play one. They want to have fun and do stuff. This is a statement more about the limits of the STs rather than the PCs, but it is an ongoing problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I've always had mixed feelings about the traditional coterie structure for PCs. While it can have its place in games, there are a lot of games where it doesn't work. PCs may wish to pursue different goals with radically different approaches, while the setting as a whole encourages betrayal and infighting.<br /> <br /> I don't know that there's a good solution for traditional tabletop games, since the GM can only spend so much time running scenes without 1+ players before the ones sitting on their hands get bored. With text-based online games, though, I've found it to be a breeze. PCs don't need to belong to the same coterie, and can go off and do their own thing in different chat rooms the GM takes turns responding to.<br /> <br /> One of my players observed to me that when PCs don't belong to the same coterie, they lose a major advantage which neonates have traditionally used to even the odds against elder vampires (strength in numbers). I think one answer is for PCs to belong to coteries of NPCs who share similar goals and methodologies to theirs, though I have yet to see the idea play out in a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one thing I do notice is that should an NPC do anything to humiliate one of the PCs, the PC will almost always allow their Humanity to fall in order to get revenge on that NPC - particularly by killing the NPC. Players really, really hate being humiliated in game. They will hate the NPC that did it with a passion that exceeds their distate for NPCs that are by far morally worse. </div> </div> </div>This is 100% true. Words I once said to a past GM after an NPC humiliated the PC I was playing:<br /> <br /> &quot;You could turn [hated NPC] into a newborn kitten and I would still want [my PC] to wring her neck. I honestly bear her even more ill will than I do [by far morally worse NPC]. I mean, [by far morally worse NPC] [does morally awful things], but that basically makes him a bogeyman. You can't hate him for being what he is, anymore than you can hate a rabid dog for biting your hand. Both need to be put down for the public good. But they're not worthy of hate, because they are incapable of being anything other than what they are. You might as well get angry at water for being wet.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;[Hated NPC] is worthy of hatred because the scope of her evil is so utterly small and petty that she should be capable of more, and yet she is not. [...] When [by far morally worse NPC] dies, it'll be a net benefit to the human race. When [hated NPC] suffers, I'll laugh with delight.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T17:35:30-07:00","id":1414845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414765#post1414765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think it depends on the group you play with and what people enjoy mostly.<br /> <br /> that being said i think most vampires fall into the Evil category from a D&amp;D point of view. At the end of day all vampires commit crimes a lot (so not lawful either though yu may say adhearing to the camarilla laws is a new kind of lawful evil)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have to be careful with the adherence to law equating to morality. For most of human history religious law and societal law are two sides of the same coin. So you could receive religious and or societal punishments for any type of crime.<br /> <br /> By many middle eastern laws anyone in the world who eats a pork product (bacon, ham, BBQ, etc) is guilty of breaking both mortal law and religious law. By Christian tradition if you eat meat on Friday you are breaking the law. Under Taliban law it was illegal to smile or laugh in public, the religious equivalent of police officers would deliver a lash with a switch to any person noticed breaking this law while they were around.<br /> <br /> Some laws are simply unjust, thus can you be considered to be a non-lawful alignment when you refuse to follow an unjust law? Yes I know that D&amp;Ds alignment system has long been a source of role playing controversy, but following the rules is not the same as being righteous.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it might be better to use the Myers Briggs 16 personality types rather than the Lawful/Neutral/Chaotic/Good/Evil paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T22:39:11-07:00","id":1414875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414845#post1414845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it might be better to use the Myers Briggs 16 personality types rather than the Lawful/Neutral/Chaotic/Good/Evil paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but that is rather unknown, the D&amp;D system is pretty much standard by roleplayers.<br /> <br /> And there lawful means upholding the LAW no matter how stupid it is. Classical Paladin trap - when the lawful action is not the good action and the good action isnt lawfull cause yes sometimes laws are wrong - but they are still laws. So lawful means abiding the law - even if the law is idiotic. It is still the rightfull thing to do by the rules of that society.<br /> <br /> So i would argue a vampire upholding the camarilla laws could still be seen as lawfull even if they violate human laws, after all a paladin is supposed to uphold the laws of his deity first, then of his nation, than other laws. So if camarilla laws conflict with human laws its lawful for a vampire to adhear to the vampiric laws first in my oppinion<br /> And clan laws first for that matter if they were to conflict with other vampiric laws<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T00:08:40-07:00","id":1414879,"title":"","content":"My answer is that the vampires who survived into neonatehood tend to be at least some measure of &quot;not nice&quot;. Because:<br /> 1. There's an element of self-selection in clan members embracing people similar to themselves. *<br /> 2. You either already are screwed up or will quickly become so if you are willing to go night to night violating people and stealing their blood.<br /> 3. By nature of the Masquerade vampires are deracinated - they are torn out of their natural community and forced into a new artificial hierarchy. That's a lot of stress.<br /> 4. Power corrupts, and a lot of vampires have the kind of power that really corrupts - blood bonding, Dominate, Presence, Obfuscate, etc. There are a lot of opportunities for vampires to embrace the worse angels of their nature.<br /> <br /> That said, I generally play vampire-on-vampire murder as rare outside of Frenzy. Every vampire has a backer in form of their sire, and death of even an unloved childe would still cost sire face. Plus unsanctioned murders violate the authority of the Prince. You may be badly beat up, but killing is a no no.<br /> <br /> My vampires lean more towards the Purple Man from Jessica Jones - they aren't vicious sociopaths, they are people given tools to spoil themselves at others' expense, who have been doing this for decades.<br /> <br /> * There's going to be a fair amount of outliers however. Not everyone is a carefully groomed successor. Some people just have a nice ass. <hr />In regards to the Baali, I stand by the assertion that no people are truly innately evil, but Baali have a baked-in Nihilism button. By the name of &quot;Daimoinon 1: Sense the Sin&quot;. At any moment, with no cost, for minimal effort, the fledgeling Baali knows exactly how screwed up everyone around them is. There is no blissful ignorance to the Baali. They know who cheats on their spouse, who steals pencils at work, who beats their husband, who forgot to feed the kids. With any person they meet, the Baali knows them at their worst. They see Evil. They do not see Good. Baali are the true clan of judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 09-21-2020, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T20:57:20-07:00","id":1415013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414875#post1414875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there lawful means upholding the LAW no matter how stupid it is. Classical Paladin trap - when the lawful action is not the good action and the good action isnt lawfull cause yes sometimes laws are wrong - but they are still laws. So lawful means abiding the law - even if the law is idiotic. It is still the rightfull thing to do by the rules of that society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except very few people or D&amp;D itself deals with the issue that there is more than one set of laws. Often those laws are contradictory to each other or simply expect to be considered first before others. A &quot;lawful&quot; character that is so inflexible as to be incapable of doing anything beyond the law isn't a character, that's OCD where the person has to stir their cup of coffee a specific number of times before drinking it.<br /> <br /> Lawful merely refers to the notion that they have a set of rules that they default to before considering alternatives or the validity of said rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T23:09:08-07:00","id":1415020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414831#post1414831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I've always had mixed feelings about the traditional coterie structure for PCs. While it can have its place in games, there are a lot of games where it doesn't work. PCs may wish to pursue different goals with radically different approaches, while the setting as a whole encourages betrayal and infighting.<br /> <br /> I don't know that there's a good solution for traditional tabletop games, since the GM can only spend so much time running scenes without 1+ players before the ones sitting on their hands get bored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if a possible solution is to allow the player (of the PC who is the odd man out) to switch from playing their PC to a second character, like an NPC ally or another PC's Retainer, who will participate in whatever group activity that would conflict against their character concept. That way they can have fun and do something as the player yet not compromise their PC.<br /> <br /> I have offered this option at least twice, but both times the players rejected it. I always thought it was a good compromise solution. Just hasn't worked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T01:20:28-07:00","id":1415028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1415020#post1415020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if a possible solution is to allow the player (of the PC who is the odd man out) to switch from playing their PC to a second character, like an NPC ally or another PC's Retainer, who will participate in whatever group activity that would conflict against their character concept. That way they can have fun and do something as the player yet not compromise their PC.<br /> <br /> I have offered this option at least twice, but both times the players rejected it. I always thought it was a good compromise solution. Just hasn't worked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essentially what Ars Magica's Troupe System is - everyone has main wizard, main non-wizard, and a bunch of expendable basket weavers. You solve the &quot;Linear Warrior, Quadratic Wizard&quot; issue by having the wizard role rotate and everyone has fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T02:58:15-07:00","id":1415036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1415013#post1415013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except very few people or D&amp;D itself deals with the issue that there is more than one set of laws. Often those laws are contradictory to each other or simply expect to be considered first before others. A &quot;lawful&quot; character that is so inflexible as to be incapable of doing anything beyond the law isn't a character, that's OCD where the person has to stir their cup of coffee a specific number of times before drinking it.<br /> <br /> Lawful merely refers to the notion that they have a set of rules that they default to before considering alternatives or the validity of said rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and that is the issue i rbought up. Cause yoru deities laws go first, then the laws of the land / society, then other laws if conflict arises. But more often than not you will be forced to either brake a law to do good or do something evil to uphold the law.<br /> <br /> Its why they changed the requirement for paladins being lawful good because it was so restricting, becaus yes, in that case you CAN NOT choose what you will do. Its more than a moral guideline.<br /> <br /> if you take the lawfulla spect nilly willy you jight as well be neutral or chaotic good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T07:54:59-07:00","id":1415070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1415020#post1415020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a possible solution is to allow the player (of the PC who is the odd man out) to switch from playing their PC to a second character, like an NPC ally or another PC's Retainer, who will participate in whatever group activity that would conflict against their character concept. That way they can have fun and do something as the player yet not compromise their PC.<br /> <br /> I have offered this option at least twice, but both times the players rejected it. I always thought it was a good compromise solution. Just hasn't worked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that players are simply more interested in playing their own PCs, much of the time. When they're playing a temporary character it's for the immediate entertainment value rather than to establish relationships or accomplish long-term goals.<br /> <br /> I have also offered that option to players several times. Sometimes they've said and sometimes they've said no. They've always done awesome jobs playing the temporary characters. However, the player isn't always able to keep doing so afterwards, and when I take over the characterization is inevitably different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T13:14:07-07:00","id":1415229,"title":"","content":"In our Dark Ages round where the characters are vampireknights of a caitiff methusalem they are as good as trained killing machines could be. Everyone of them has easy a kill of their age per year but all of those where done against other people with a weapon. The innocent and those that surrender where always spared by them.<br /> <br /> In our modern nights session the characters are mostly survivors, where they do what they need to survive another night but do not go out of their way to kill or harm people. If there is violence done, it is mostly either provoked by the other side or some tragic accident.<br /> <br /> In our mage round the TL of my character is a kindhearted maiden who sometimes even regret their goodness because she can not bring herself to go predator and help her love in the fights but stay at her home being just a blood drinking sorceror that only wait for her beloved to come back to her while always fearing that everytime when she goes to sleep an SEK stormes the door and kills her for just being cursed despite she never did something like what the rest of her kind is infamous for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T01:40:11-07:00","id":1415658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1414879#post1414879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In regards to the Baali, I stand by the assertion that no people are truly innately evil, but Baali have a baked-in Nihilism button. By the name of &quot;Daimoinon 1: Sense the Sin&quot;. At any moment, with no cost, for minimal effort, the fledgeling Baali knows exactly how screwed up everyone around them is. There is no blissful ignorance to the Baali. They know who cheats on their spouse, who steals pencils at work, who beats their husband, who forgot to feed the kids. With any person they meet, the Baali knows them at their worst. They see Evil. They do not see Good. Baali are the true clan of judges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, now this is neat.<br /> <br /> In the last season of Buffy, there were a group called 'the Bringers' who gouged out their own eyes and only 'saw' via the illusions that their evil big bad master fed them, and, naturally, said visions were twisted to paint the world as the master wanted them to see it, so that a champion of good they saw as a horrific thing that must be destroyed. I like that Sense the Sin kind of perpetuates the evil, by showing only the world at it's worst, and 'proving' to the Baali that all people are horrible and corrupt and so it's totally normal to be equally depraved and to hold them all in contempt, because the magic flashlight conveniently doesn't show them the older brother being super-protective of his disabled kid brother, or the love of a nanny for the child she's watching, or any of the better parts of the human experience. All they get to see is the ugly, and they embrace the ugly, since, as far as they can see, that's all that there is in the world...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T03:42:53-07:00","id":1415666,"title":"","content":"The funny thing about Sense the sin, at least in DAV20 ( easily the best writup of Daimonion) is that it works in accordance to what path someone's taking, so if you used it on someone on the Path of Bones you might get stuff like 'I indulged in a beautiful midnight stroll' or 'you could find someone on the Path of Typhon guilty of giving someone &quot;sound moral advice&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly I think if you were to sense-the-sin on a lot of people (not a great idea) you'd just get laughable petty stuff (like pencil stealing), and what's pencil stealing in comparison to child molesters? The majority of people are boring. The majority of people are nuerotypical... of course vampires are generally operating among society's extremes (The very poor and the very rich) so we can throw that out of the window, but vampires know they're doing that. <br /> <br /> I feel like having sense the sin would actually have me trust people<i> more</i> than I would as a vampire with other disciplines (except Dominate 4, that one's great for trust). If I know people at their worst and what dark secrets they hide, I know who to trust (And it certainly helps that I know what buttons to push)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T09:25:06-07:00","id":1415694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414571-the-morality-thread-how-evil-are-your-kindred?p=1415666#post1415666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think if you were to sense-the-sin on a lot of people (not a great idea) you'd just get laughable petty stuff (like pencil stealing), and what's pencil stealing in comparison to child molesters? The majority of people are boring. The majority of people are nuerotypical... of course vampires are generally operating among society's extremes (The very poor and the very rich) so we can throw that out of the window, but vampires know they're doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people are not introspective enough to realize their sins so there is a fair amount of leeway as to what would be their actual worst sin. Is it the one they actively know of or the ones which they didn't realize caused far more collateral damage.<br /> <br /> This is further complicated by time. Such as a Parent who sent their kids to Sunday school, only find out 10-20 years later that there were several pedophile priests stationed there at the time. The initial act of believing in the institution isn't a sin, nor is that act sending the kids there, but the fact you find out about it later on means our human psychology retroactively changes our moral assessments of our guilt.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if the Disciplines are using ST level knowledge to pinpoint the greatest sin of a given person regardless if they are aware of it or not, then most people you use it on will pop up with something like &quot;I contributed to climate change which killed hundreds if not thousands of people&quot; just because of the tangential connections of so many catastrophes and the body counts that rack up over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T10:59:11-07:00","id":1415700,"title":"","content":"I think Sense the Sin is too powerful for a level 1 Discipline. My character wouldn\u2019t want some random neonate being able to know her deepest secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T12:19:14-07:00","id":1415715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container